.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
. *** H4: Having daughters leads to a larger increase in the support of gender 
> equality for men than for women (with gender equality measured by attitudes).
>  *** 
. 
.         /* Verbal description of your model: Gender of first child is exogene
> ous, later children may be endogeneous. Regress the outcome on dummy variable
>  indicating whether the first child is a daughter, for parents. Include indic
> ators for survey years because of time trends and because some outcomes may b
> e combinations of variables from different years. Cluster standard errors on 
> individual respondent.  */ 
. 
.         * Regression  
. 
.         reg gender_equality d_daughter d_daughter_men sex i.syear, vce(cl pid
> )

